{"seq":2,"slug":"biochemistry-molecular","title":"第二章 生物化学与分子基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/medicine/basic-medicine/biochemistry-molecular","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"proteins-and-enzymes","title":"大学基础医学 — 蛋白质与酶","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/medicine/basic-medicine/biochemistry-molecular/proteins-and-enzymes","wordCount":1872,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"metabolism-and-energy","title":"大学基础医学 — 代谢与能量","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/medicine/basic-medicine/biochemistry-molecular/metabolism-and-energy","wordCount":1832,"readingTime":8},{"seq":3,"slug":"gene-expression","title":"大学基础医学 — 基因与遗传信息","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/medicine/basic-medicine/biochemistry-molecular/gene-expression","wordCount":2020,"readingTime":9}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"第二章-生物化学与分子基础\">第二章 生物化学与分子基础</h1><p>本章把视角从器官、细胞进一步缩小到分子层面，回答一个根本问题：生命活动的化学本质是什么？我们将认识构成生命的核心分子——蛋白质、酶，理解能量如何在细胞中产生和流转，以及遗传信息如何从 DNA 一路转化为具体的生命功能。</p>\n<p>生物化学是连接&quot;结构&quot;与&quot;疾病&quot;的桥梁。许多疾病（如糖尿病、苯丙酮尿症、遗传病）的本质，都是某个分子、某条代谢通路或某个基因出了问题。掌握分子机制，你才能真正理解疾病&quot;为什么会发生&quot;，而不只是&quot;表现为什么&quot;。</p>\n"}